From: RicemanRhys <176650384+RicemanRhys@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:15:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Local-only: xbox_d3d8 can time its D3D11 context calls for a
 caller that asks (d3d8_ctx_timing; measurement only, the calls made as
 before; twoc step 95)

The COM macros for the context calls the draws, uploads, copies and binds use (Map, Unmap, Draw, DrawIndexed, the IA / VS / PS / RS / OM sets, UpdateSubresource, the copies, clears and resolves) go through inline wrappers in d3d8_internal.h: while d3d8_ctx_timing is nonzero each call is timed with QueryPerformanceCounter into d3d8_ctx_ticks and counted in d3d8_ctx_calls; otherwise it costs a load and a branch. VSSetConstantBuffers1 (the constants ring) is timed at its one call site. The smoke tests' stubs define the three globals.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
